cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the associated article and this repository."
title: "Code and data for: Surrogate Attribution in Hybrid Quantum–Classical QAOA for Discrete–Continuous Energy Hub Design"
type: software
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
license: MIT
abstract: "Code, data and figures behind the manuscript “Surrogate Attribution in Hybrid Quantum–Classical QAOA for Discrete–Continuous Energy Hub Design”. Two fully enumerable discrete–continuous benchmarks (Energy Hub design, N = 18 technologies, K = 6; cardinality-constrained mean–variance portfolio, N = 15 assets, K = 5), their exhaustive references, the exact-cardinality QAOA samplers, the controls and the analysis and figure scripts. Code: MIT License; data, results and figures: CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DATA.md)."
